      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFor hybrid attention/mamba models, round the block size derived from the mamba state up to a multiple of `--prefix-match-unit` instead of failing at startup. AI assistance (Claude Code) was used to prepare this PR; I reviewed every changed line.\n\n## Claims\n\n- The derived size is often divisor-poor (2112 tokens for Qwen3.5-35B-A3B with fp8 KV), so most units failed:\n  ```\n  ValueError: Invalid prefix_match_unit=256; prefix-cacheable KV cache group block sizes must be divisible by prefix_match_unit. Got group block sizes=[2112, 2112, 2112, 2112], ...\n  ```\n- Units that already divide it are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n```\n$ pytest tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_model_runner.py -k rounds_up_to_prefix_match_unit\n3 passed                                    # this PR (CPU and GB300)\n1 failed, 2 passed                          # main\nE       AssertionError: assert 400 == 512\n```\n\nGB300, Qwen3.5-35B-A3B, fp8 KV, `prefix_match_unit=256`: starts with this PR (block size 2112 → 2304), fails on `main`.\n\n## Details\n\nThe step is `lcm(kernel alignment, backend alignment, prefix_match_unit)`. The mamba page is padded to the attention page anyway; this adds a little more padding, and a warning is logged when it grows the block by more than 10%. The `prefix_match_unit` docstring mentions the rounding.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
